        {
          "id": "20c12e88-68da-4e93-8282-23ac779a27e0",
          "body": "Batch 020 manual primary-PDF extraction. Methods, Table 1, Table 2, Figures 1-3, results, and discussion were checked (article pp. 201-209). The direct layout is all seasons followed by the eight reported seasons. Table 1 supports season-level team, age, and exposure rows; headline injury/illness outcomes and Table 2 metrics are pooled-only and remain on All seasons. Table 2 reports medians (IQR) rather than means in its structured severity columns; values are labelled accordingly. The source reports illness incidence/system percentages but no total illness count, so no illness count or structured system count was inferred. Table 2 is intentionally not aggregated across incomplete location/type subsets.",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-13T00:11:20.981+00:00"
        },
        {
          "id": "2a78e5dc-1a63-4d77-a92d-bdb0466daed3",
          "body": "Aspetar professional QSL anchor reconciliation, 2026-07-27. Existing S2824 All seasons and 2014/15-2021/22 rows remain the modern all-injury denominator. Added source-scoped rows: disjoint 2008/09 S195 all-injury cohort; overlapping S344 groin, S555 ACL, and S712 head/neck-concussion topic supplements. Topic rows must not be summed as independent all-injury denominators. S544 and S3577 are covered by the S344 row and remain audit-only secondary analyses.",
